      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your desire to feel better quickly, but taking a higher dose of a leftover antibiotic could be dangerous. Even if your previous infection was bacterial, each illness is unique, and there's no guarantee that it's the same this time. Overdosing on antibiotics can cause severe side effects, such as allergic reactions or damage to your kidneys. It's crucial to use antibiotics only under the guidance of a healthcare professional. Try to find another way to resolve your symptoms, and don't hesitate to reach out to a medical clinic or clinic in advance if you have difficulty getting an appointment immediately. Your health should be carefully managed to prevent further complications.",
